escalated", "relay": "The change in chemical potential is +7.3 kJ mol⁻¹.", "expert_answer": "(b) +7.3 kJ mol$^{-1}$", "expert_latency_s": 2.09, "stall_ms": 21, "relay_ms": 1732}
{"id": "q0235", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 72.44, "n_chunks": 73, "scores": [0.7783, 0.6884, 0.7972, 0.7225, 0.7139, 0.7114, 0.71, 0.7335, 0.6545, 0.5841, 0.7551, 0.4345, 0.7182, 0.7152, 0.6819, 0.3862, 0.8102, 0.2714, 0.6034, 0.6017, 0.563, 0.5377, 0.4122, 0.4381, 0.5189, 0.7449, 0.6959, 0.4183, 0.4053, 0.5269, 0.5843, 0.6738, 0.6647, 0.5768, 0.5988, 0.6592, 0.6623, 0.7151, 0.6934, 0.6836, 0.709, 0.6773, 0.6663, 0.7483, 0.7942, 0.7144, 0.7459, 0.6745, 0.6911, 0.5755, 0.7729, 0.746, 0.7889, 0.8066, 0.6647, 0.6328, 0.7114, 0.7089, 0.7472, 0.7359, 0.5941, 0.7313, 0.6278, 0.7431, 0.71, 0.5941, 0.6782, 0.734, 0.514, 0.7207, 0.6477, 0.796, 0.6645], "eot_score": 0.4719, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "G. Burials with exotic grave goods also contain bones indicating that they engaged in less strenuous labor.", "query": "Which of the following is archaeological evidence of social stratification and inequality?\n\nA. Burials with exotic grave goods also contain bones indicating that they engaged in more strenuous labor.\nB. Burials all contain equal amounts of exotic grave goods, but some are more impressive than others.\nC. Burials without exotic grave goods also contain bones indicating that they engaged in strenuous labor.\nD. Burials all contain bones indicating that they engaged in same level of strenuous labor.\nE. Burials contain bones indicating that people were segregated based on gender, stature, and personal capabilities, including artistic abilities.\nF. All burials contain equal amounts of non-exotic grave goods.\nG. Burials with exotic grave goods also contain bones indicating that they engaged in less strenuous labor.\nH. Burials contain bones indicating that people were segregated based on their age and health.\nI. Burials without exotic grave goods also contain bones indicating that they engaged in less strenuous labor.\nJ. Burials contain only exotic grave goods with no indication of the deceased's labor.\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "transcript": "Which of the following is archaeological evidence of social stratification and inequality? (A) Burials with exotic grave goods also contain bones indicating that they engaged in more strenuous labor. (B) Burials all contain equal amounts of exotic grave goods but some are more impressive than others. (C) Burials without exotic grave goods also contain bones indicating that they engaged in strenuous labor. (D) Burials all contain bones indicating that they engaged in same level of strenuous labor. (E) Burials contain bones indicating that people were segregated based on gender, stature, and personal capabilities, including artistic abilities. (F) All burials contain equal amounts of non-exotic grave goods. (G) Burials with exotic grave goods also contain bones indicating that they engaged in less strenuous labor. (H) Burials contain bones indicating that people were segregated based on their age and health. (I) Burials without exotic grave goods also contain bones indicating that they engaged in less strenuous labor. (J) Burials contain only exotic grave goods with no indication of the deceased's labor. Answer with the correct option letter and its content.", "first_audio_ms": 547, "spoken_s": 5.04, "mode": "local", "answer": "B. Burials all contain exotic grave goods, but some are more impressive than others.", "answer_ms": 2018}
{"id": "q0241", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 37.66, "n_chunks": 38, "scores": [0.7405, 0.807, 0.8273, 0.7293, 0.6512, 0.7148, 0.7191, 0.6138, 0.6294, 0.5826, 0.4567, 0.5744, 0.6435, 0.6179, 0.6547, 0.5403, 0.7398, 0.7135, 0.5137, 0.6193, 0.7226, 0.4889, 0.6889, 0.7662, 0.6934, 0.6799, 0.6876, 0.6341, 0.7571, 0.7679, 0.6549, 0.7756, 0.7988, 0.6453, 0.7091, 0.7238, 0.8282, 0.7538], "eot_score": 0.6127, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "D. Economic, Legal, Ethical and Philanthropic", "query": "According Carroll what four categories or aspects can corporate social responsibility be broken down into?\n\nA. Political, Legal, Ethical and Philanthropic\nB. Economic, Legal, Ethical and Moral\nC. Economic, Legal, Ethical and Environmental\nD. Economic, Legal, Ethical and Philanthropic\nE. Political, Legal, Cultural and Philanthropic\nF. Economic, Legal, Humanitarian and Philanthropic\nG. Economic, Legal, Cultural and Philanthropic\nH. Economic, Cultural, Ethical and Environmental\nI. Political, Legal, Economic and Environmental\nJ. Political, Legal, Ethical and Environmental\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "transcript": "According to Carroll, what four categories or aspects can corporate social responsibility be broken down into? A) political, legal, ethical, and philanthropic. B) economic, legal, ethical, and moral. C) economic, legal, ethical, and environmental. D) economic, legal, ethical, and philanthropic. E) political, legal, cultural, and philanthropic. F) economic, legal, humanitarian, and philanthropic. G) economic, legal, cultural, and philanthropic. H) economic, cultural, ethical, and environmental. I) political, legal, economic, and environmental. J) political, legal, ethical, and environmental. Answer with the correct option letter and its content.", "first_audio_ms": 550, "spoken_s": 4.2, "mode": "local", "answer": "J. Political, legal, ethical, and environmental.", "answer_ms": 1580}
{"id": "q0247", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 67.31, "n_chunks": 68, "scores": [0.7673, 0.7762, 0.7504, 0.8263, 0.2726, 0.6241, 0.7871, 0.6787, 0.7768, 0.45, 0.7564, 0.3788, 0.5882, 0.7121, 0.724, 0.5919, 0.7123, 0.6287, 0.7499, 0.5489, 0.6616, 0.6461, 0.5215, 0.6521, 0.6224, 0.6291, 0.4381, 0.3136, 0.2699, 0.6114, 0.6771, 0.6498, 0.3288, 0.6529, 0.5191, 0.3928, 0.691, 0.7214, 0.6283, 0.4575, 0.686, 0.7086, 0.6493, 0.5965, 0.4024, 0.6739, 0.7038, 0.5643, 0.5629, 0.5205, 0.468, 0.7191, 0.6868, 0.6172, 0.3872, 0.5033, 0.5557, 0.7166, 0.6227, 0.6328, 0.3939, 0.4737, 0.4435, 0.269, 0.7026, 0.6384, 0.4724, 0.6518], "eot_score": 0.5241, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "B. Parallel storage allows simultaneous storage of information, activating it from different sources after an experience and contributing to both memory and thinking.", "query": "Why are parallel memory codes so important in the understanding of the role of memory in thought?\n\nA. Parallel storage duplicates information across different brain regions, leading to multiple identical memories\nB. Parallel storage allows simultaneous storage of information, activating it from different sources after an experience and contributing to both memory and thinking.\nC. Parallel storage enables the brain to process information sequentially rather than simultaneously\nD. Parallel storage helps in storing large volumes of data\nE. Parallel storage helps in quickly retrieving information\nF. Parallel storage helps in organizing information\nG. Parallel storage increases the brain's reliance on single-threaded processing\nH. Parallel storage compresses data for compact storage, but does not affect thinking\nI. Parallel storage ensures complete accuracy in memory recall without any distortions\nJ. Parallel storage is important for creating long-term memories, but has no impact on immediate thought processes\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "transcript": "Why are parallel memory codes so important in the understanding of the role of memory and thought? A. Parallel storage duplicates information across different brain regions, leading to multiple identical memories. B. Parallel storage allows simultaneous storage of information, activating it from different sources after an experience and contributing to both memory and thinking. C. Parallel storage enables the brain to process information sequentially rather than simultaneously. D. Parallel storage helps in storing large volumes of data. E. Parallel storage helps in quickly retrieving information. F. Parallel storage helps in organizing information. G. Parallel storage increases the brain's reliance on single-threaded processing. H. Parallel storage compresses data for compact storage but does not affect thinking. I. Parallel storage ensures complete accuracy in memory recall without any distortions. J. Parallel storage is important for creating long-term memories but has no impact on immediate thought processes. Answer with the correct option letter and its content.", "first_audio_ms": 547, "spoken_s": 9.56, "mode": "local", "answer": "B. Parallel storage allows simultaneous storage of information, activating it from different sources after an experience and contributing to both memory and thinking.", "answer_ms": 3748}
{"id": "q0255", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 77.4, "n_chunks": 78, "scores": [0.9999, 0.6875, 0.6956, 0.7979, 0.7987, 0.7231, 0.8299, 0.7828, 0.8117, 0.7222, 0.8103, 0.6594, 0.5794, 0.7253, 0.7132, 0.7364, 0.6914, 0.7459, 0.7515, 0.7246, 0.7276, 0.7429, 0.707, 0.4361, 0.8182, 0.7954, 0.7798, 0.6921, 0.7108, 0.6788, 0.6137, 0.6794, 0.464, 0.7321, 0.7269, 0.6685, 0.6698, 0.7556, 0.7014, 0.6627, 0.6786, 0.7445, 0.6812, 0.6277, 0.7135, 0.7218, 0.56, 0.7002, 0.6398, 0.7308, 0.7044, 0.7007, 0.7256, 0.6986, 0.4965, 0.7177, 0.7447, 0.5944, 0.7588, 0.7553, 0.6104, 0.6091, 0.7381, 0.7062, 0.6424, 0.7432, 0.75, 0.7623, 0.7387, 0.7176, 0.772, 0.7367, 0.6985, 0.6092, 0.7946, 0.7868, 0.8388, 0.7008], "eot_score": 0.5511, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "I. admissible as an admission.", "query": "A college student and a man got into a fight at a bar while playing pooi. The college student allegedly started the fight when he struck the man in the head with a pool cue after the man sank a game-winning shot. At the college student's trial for assault, the prosecution called one of the college student's classmates to testify. The classmate was not at the bar during the fight. The classmate offered to testify that the next day at class, he approached the college student and said, \"It was wrong of you to start a fight with the man over a game of pool,\" at which point, the college student bowed his head and walked away. The classmate's testimony is\n\nA. admissible as a statement of the declarant’s then-existing state of mind.\nB. inadmissible as a character evidence.\nC. inadmissible as hearsay not within any recognized exception.\nD. admissible as a prior consistent statement.\nE. inadmissible as a statement that is not in the defendant's favor.\nF. inadmissible because the classmate was not an eyewitness to the fight.\nG. inadmissible as self-serving.\nH. admissible as part of the res gestae.\nI. admissible as an admission.\nJ. admissible as a statement of personal or family history.\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "transcript": "A college student and a man got into a fight at a bar while playing pool. The college student allegedly started the fight when he struck the man in the head with a pool cue after the man sank a game-winning shot. At the college student's trial for assault, the prosecution called one of the college student's classmates to testify. The classmate was not at the bar during the fight. The classmate offered to testify that the next day at class, he approached the college student and said, \"It was wrong of you to start a fight with the man over a game of pool,\" at which point the college student bowed his head and walked away. The classmate's testimony is A) admissible as a statement of the declarant's then-existing state of mind. B) inadmissible as character evidence. C) inadmissible as hearsay not within any recognized exception. D) admissible as a prior consistent statement. E) inadmissible as a statement that is not in the defendant's favor. F) inadmissible because the classmate was not an eyewitness to the fight. G) inadmissible as self-serving. H) admissible as part of the res gestae. I) admissible as an admission. J) admissible as a statement of personal or family history. Answer with the correct option letter and its content.", "first_audio_ms": 551, "spoken_s": 4.84, "mode": "local", "answer": "A. Admissible as a statement of the declarant's then-existing state of mind.", "answer_ms": 2030}
{"id": "q0264", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 150.71, "n_chunks": 151, "scores": [0.6743, 0.6908, 0.7336, 0.7229, 0.8147, 0.7447, 0.7841, 0.7887, 0.8095, 0.8416, 0.778, 0.7932, 0.7752, 0.7673, 0.6653, 0.5908, 0.8583, 0.7335, 0.7395, 0.7237, 0.7157, 0.684, 0.716, 0.7769, 0.716, 0.702, 0.7477, 0.723, 0.7704, 0.7086, 0.7587, 0.5853, 0.829, 0.8209, 0.4655, 0.7666, 0.7444, 0.5876, 0.7466, 0.7301, 0.8565, 0.823, 0.776, 0.6732, 0.6683, 0.7967, 0.7294, 0.7211, 0.7582, 0.7812, 0.7671, 0.7207, 0.7887, 0.824, 0.7994, 0.8173, 0.8178, 0.7805, 0.7487, 0.8349, 0.7403, 0.7578, 0.7818, 0.8161, 0.8243, 0.6898, 0.8291, 0.7277, 0.849, 0.8069, 0.7916, 0.7992, 0.8384, 0.8242, 0.7898, 0.8502, 0.7966, 0.7464, 0.7156, 0.651, 0.8191, 0.8347, 0.8268, 0.7982, 0.8232, 0.819, 0.8799, 0.8023, 0.5443, 0.635, 0.7301, 0.7235, 0.8572, 0.7785, 0.7009, 0.787, 0.7078, 0.7731, 0.7585, 0.6004, 0.7706, 0.7918, 0.8079, 0.7015, 0.7308, 0.8244, 0.7819, 0.7255, 0.7031, 0.6922, 0.7338, 0.7501, 0.6179, 0.6788, 0.7033, 0.8303, 0.7563, 0.746, 0.7114, 0.766, 0.7918, 0.7144, 0.7574, 0.649, 0.7626, 0.7257, 0.7621, 0.7724, 0.694, 0.7892, 0.6367, 0.8018, 0.7673, 0.8176, 0.7669, 0.8373, 0.7171, 0.6966, 0.7637, 0.7825, 0.7407, 0.7756, 0.7584, 0.7353, 0.7847, 0.7144, 0.6621, 0.7483, 0.7794, 0.7046, 0.8093], "eot_score": 0.7821, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "B. not recover, because the professor remains liable.", "query": "A landlord owned a three-story home in fee simple and leased it to his friend for a term of 10 years. By the terms of the lease, the friend expressly covenanted to pay a monthly rental of $300 and to pay the taxes on the premises during the term of the lease. The lease also stipulated that the friend, as lessee, may not assign or sublease the said premises. The friend and his family lived in the house for two years. Then the friend, still owing the landlord three months back rent, assigned his leasehold interest in the property to a professor, who was unaware of the prohibition against assignments. This written assignment expressly provided that the professor would pay the landlord the monthly rental of $300, but was silent concerning the payment of taxes. The landlord never objected to this assignment. Six months after the assignment, the landlord conveyed his property interest in the premises to a new owner. After residing in the house for a year, the professor subleased the third floor to a student for a term of two years; the agreement provided that the professor would receive a monthly rental payment of $100. After the student had made regular rental payments to the professor for the first six months of the sublease, he defaulted. The following month, the professor sent the new owner $200 as payment for rent and notified him that he should collect the remaining $100 from the student, who refused to vacate the premises. In an action by the new owner against the student to recover the additional $100 for rent due, he will most probably\n\nA. recover, even though he never objected to the sublease.\nB. not recover, because the professor remains liable.\nC. recover, because the new owner inherited all rights and responsibilities from the original landlord.\nD. recover, because the landlord and sublessee are in privity of estate.\nE. not recover, because the student is not directly responsible to the new owner.\nF. not recover, because the student was not in privity of contract with the new owner.\nG. not recover, because the professor would only be held liable.\nH. not recover, because the professor is the one who subleased to the student.\nI. recover, because the student is in direct violation of his sublease agreement.\nJ. recover, because the student defaulted on his rental payment.\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "transcript": "A landlord owned a three-story home in fee simple and leased it to his friend for a term of ten years. By the terms of the lease, the friend expressly covenanted to pay a monthly rental of three hundred dollars and to pay the taxes on the premises during the term of the lease. The lease also stipulated that the friend, as lessee, may not assign or sublease the said premises. The friend and his family lived in the house for two years. Then the friend, still owing the landlord three months back rent, assigned his leasehold interest in the property to a professor, who was unaware of the prohibition against assignments. This written assignment expressly provided that the professor would pay the landlord the monthly rental of three hundred dollars, but was silent concerning the payment of taxes. The landlord never objected to this assignment. Six months after the assignment, the landlord conveyed his property interest in the premises to a new owner. After residing in the house for a year, the professor subleased the third floor to a student for a term of two years. The agreement provided that the professor would receive a monthly rental payment of one hundred dollars. After the student had made regular rental payments to the professor for the first six months of the sublease, he defaulted. The following month, the professor sent the new owner two hundred dollars as payment for rent and notified him that he should collect the remaining one hundred dollars from the student, who refused to vacate the premises. In an action by the new owner against the student to recover the additional one hundred dollars for rent due, he will most probably A) recover, even though he never objected to the sublease. B) not recover, because the professor remains liable. C) recover, because the new owner inherited all rights and responsibilities from the original landlord. D) recover, because the landlord and sublessee are in privity of estate. E) not recover, because the student is not directly responsible to the new owner. F) not recover, because the student was not in privity of contract with the new owner. G) not recover, because the professor would only be held liable. H) not recover, because the professor is the one who subleased to the student. I) recover, because the student is in direct violation of his sublease agreement. J) recover, because the student defaulted on his rental payment.", "first_audio_ms": 21, "stall_pcm_s": 3.2, "relay_first_audio_ms": 588, "spoken_s": 16.56, "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The new owner likely won't be able to recover the $100 from the student. Since the student is just a sublessee, there's no direct legal connection between them and the new owner—no privity of estate or contract. The professor remains responsible for paying the full rent to the new owner.", "expert_answer": "E) not recover, because the student is not directly responsible to the new owner.\n\nThe student is a sublessee, so there is no privity of estate or privity of contract between the student and the new owner. The professor remains liable to the new owner for the full rent.", "expert_latency_s": 5.93, "stall_ms": 21, "relay_ms": 7058}
{"id": "q0271", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 29.89, "n_chunks": 30, "scores": [0.7336, 0.7881, 0.7656, 0.8513, 0.7987, 0.7421, 0.8286, 0.6851, 0.7422, 0.5384, 0.8048, 0.8323, 0.7863, 0.8075, 0.7528, 0.7826, 0.6383, 0.8411, 0.828, 0.8327, 0.7491, 0.7934, 0.7832, 0.7764, 0.7957, 0.7478, 0.8338, 0.796, 0.8751, 0.8348], "eot_score": 0.8607, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "C. 700 and 900", "query": "Estimate 999 - 103. The difference is between which numbers?\n\nA. 500 and 700\nB. 200 and 400\nC. 700 and 900\nD. 1,300 and 1,500\nE. 800 and 1,000\nF. 900 and 1,100\nG. 400 and 600\nH. 100 and 300\nI. 600 and 800\nJ. 1,000 and 1,200\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "transcript": "Estimate nine hundred ninety nine hundred and three. The differences between which numbers? a) five hundred and seven hundred, b) two hundred and four hundred, c) seven hundred and nine hundred, d) one thousand three hundred and one thousand five hundred, e) eight hundred and one thousand, f) nine hundred and one thousand, g) four hundred and six hundred, h) one hundred and three hundred, i) six hundred and eight hundred, j) one thousand and twelve hundred. Answer with the correct option letter and its content.", "first_audio_ms": 20, "stall_pcm_s": 3.2, "relay_first_audio_ms": 573, "spoken_s": 3.72, "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The numbers with the smallest difference are nine hundred and one thousand.", "expert_answer": "f) nine hundred and one thousand", "expert_latency_s": 9.4, "stall_ms": 20, "relay_ms": 1587}
{"id": "q0287", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 17.29, "n_chunks": 18, "scores": [0.5395, 0.828, 0.4599, 0.6397, 0.2918, 0.5388, 0.482, 0.452, 0.545, 0.5372, 0.6388, 0.6076, 0.5701, 0.4307, 0.6937, 0.6461, 0.6799, 0.5449], "eot_score": 0.3261, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "I. 25%", "query": "A sofa has a markup of 20% based on its selling price. Find the percent markup based on the cost.\n\nA. 28%\nB. 15%\nC. 22%\nD. 10%\nE. 30%\nF. 20%\nG. 40%\nH. 18%\nI. 25%\nJ. 35%\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "transcript": "A sofa has a markup of twenty percent based on its selling price. Find the percent markup based on the cost. (A) twenty-eight percent (B) fifteen percent (C) twenty-two percent (D) ten percent (E) thirty percent (F) twenty percent (G) forty percent (H) eighteen percent (I) (J) thirty-five percent. Answer with the correct option letter and its content.", "first_audio_ms": 552, "spoken_s": 468.4, "mode": "local", "answer": "We are told that the markup is 20% based on the **selling price**. Let’s define the variables clearly to find the markup based on **cost** as a percentage of cost, i.e., percent markup based on cost = $\\frac{\\text{markup}}{\\text{cost}} \\times 100\\% $ or simply the ratio of markup to cost expressed as a percentage of cost. But let's proceed step by step using algebra or logic with percentages. Let the **selling price** be $ S $. Given that markup is 20% **based on the selling price**, that means the markup is 20% of the selling price. So, markup = $ 0.20 \\times S $. Now, recall that selling price = cost + markup. So, $ S = C + \\text{markup} $, where $ C $ is the cost. Substituting the expression for markup, we get $ S = C + 0.20S $. Solve for $ C $ in terms of $ S $, then find the markup as a percent of cost. Rearranging the equation above, we have $ S - 0.20S = C $, so $ 0.80S = C $. Thus, the cost is 80% of the selling price. The markup is 20% of the selling price. So, markup based on cost is $ \\frac{\\text{markup}}{\\text{cost}} \\times 100\\% = \\frac{0.20S}{0.80S} \\times 100\\% = \\frac{0.20}{0.80} \\times 100\\% = 0.25 \\times 100\\% = 25\\% $? Wait, that doesn't match any options? Let me check again. Wait, maybe I misinterpreted the problem. Let me read again. \"Markup of 20 percent based on its selling price.\" That means markup = 20% of selling price. So, if S is selling price, then markup = 0.20S. Then cost = S - markup = S - 0.20S = 0.80S. So, cost is 0.80S. Now, markup as a percent of cost is $ \\frac{0.20S}{0.80S} \\times 100\\", "answer_ms": 183172}
{"id": "q0306", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 4.21, "n_chunks": 5, "scores": [0.998, 0.6366, 0.6396, 0.6835, 0.5994], "eot_score": 0.3802, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "John Alcock and Arthur Brown", "query": "Who were the first men to fly the Atlantic non stop in 1919", "transcript": "Who were the first men to fly the Atlantic non-stop in nineteen nineteen?", "first_audio_ms": 557, "spoken_s": 22.64, "mode": "local", "answer": "The first men to fly across the Atlantic non-stop in 1919 were British aviators John Alcock and Arthur Whitten Brown. They completed the historic flight on June 14, 1919, flying a modified Vickers Vimy bomber from St. John's, Newfoundland, to Clifden, Ireland—marking one of the earliest successful transatlantic flights without refueling en route.", "answer_ms": 9850}
{"id": "q0310", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 7.19, "n_chunks": 8, "scores": [0.7127, 0.6202, 0.5229, 0.7625, 0.8202, 0.5905, 0.6309, 0.6969], "eot_score": 0.6466, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "RAYMOND BENSON", "query": "The character 'James Bond' was created by Ian Fleming, but who wrote the book 'Zero Minus Ten' featuring 'James Bond'?", "transcript": "The character James Bond was created by Ian Fleming, but who wrote the book Zero Minus Ten featuring James Bond?", "first_audio_ms": 29, "stall_pcm_s": 3.2, "relay_first_audio_ms": 602, "spoken_s": 5.56, "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Raymond Benson wrote *Zero Minus Ten*, the James Bond novel.", "expert_answer": "Raymond Benson wrote *Zero Minus Ten*, the James Bond novel.", "expert_latency_s": 2.46, "stall_ms": 29, "relay_ms": 2245}
{"id": "q0316", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 4.17, "n_chunks": 5, "scores": [0.6619, 0.7749, 0.6845, 0.5643, 0.7148], "eot_score": 0.3818, "eot_read_ms": 22, "reference_answer": "Vision", "query": "In medicine, chromotopsia is the term for abnormally coloured what?", "transcript": "In medicine, chromatopsia is the term for abnormally colored what?", "first_audio_ms": 559, "spoken_s": 21.0, "mode": "local", "answer": "In medicine, chromatopsia is the term for abnormally colored **vision** or more specifically, **abnormal color vision**. It refers to a condition where colors appear distorted or different from normal—either overly intense, faded, or altered in hue and saturation—often due to neurological or visual system disorders.", "answer_ms": 9156}
{"id": "q0333", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.1, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.9992, 0.795, 0.5492, 0.7211], "eot_score": 0.3631, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Quirt", "query": "What is the name given to a short handled riding stick", "transcript": "What is the name given to a short handled riding stick?", "first_audio_ms": 561, "spoken_s": 10.08, "mode": "local", "answer": "A short-handled riding stick is commonly known as a **crop**. It is used in horse riding to help guide the horse, typically by tapping near its hindquarters or legs.", "answer_ms": 4163}
{"id": "q0349", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 8.35, "n_chunks": 9, "scores": [1.0, 0.7672, 0.768, 0.8584, 0.7288, 0.6494, 0.8082, 0.6434, 0.696], "eot_score": 0.4602, "eot_read_ms": 22, "reference_answer": "Blue Riband", "query": "What name is given to the unofficial accolade awarded to the fastest passenger ship to cross the Atlantic in the westbound direction?", "transcript": "What name is given to the unofficial accolade awarded to the fastest passenger ship to cross the Atlantic in the westbound direction?", "first_audio_ms": 603, "spoken_s": 21.12, "mode": "local", "answer": "The unofficial accolade awarded to the fastest passenger ship to cross the Atlantic in the westbound direction is commonly known as **\"Blue Riband.\"** This prestigious title recognizes outstanding speed and performance on transatlantic voyages. Historically, it was associated with ocean liners competing for supremacy during the golden age of steamship travel.", "answer_ms": 8961}
{"id": "q0356", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 5.67, "n_chunks": 6, "scores": [0.8037, 0.7902, 0.7406, 0.7996, 0.7996, 0.7116], "eot_score": 0.6616, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "CHARLES GOUNOD", "query": "Who, more famous for his opera ‘Faust’, wrote the music used for the anthem of the Vatican City?", "transcript": "Who, more famous for his opera Faust, wrote the music used for the anthem of the Vatican City?", "first_audio_ms": 29, "stall_pcm_s": 3.2, "relay_first_audio_ms": 628, "spoken_s": 9.76, "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The music used for the anthem of Vatican City was composed by Charles Gounod, who's famous for his opera *Faust*.", "expert_answer": "Charles Gounod, the French composer best known for the opera *Faust*, wrote the music used for the anthem of Vatican City.", "expert_latency_s": 2.82, "stall_ms": 29, "relay_ms": 4136}
{"id": "q0363", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.67, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.8758, 0.6845, 0.7602], "eot_score": 0.628, "eot_read_ms": 23, "reference_answer": "Cornwall", "query": "Yarg and gevrik are cheeses from which county?", "transcript": "Yarg and Gevrek are cheeses from which county?", "first_audio_ms": 22, "stall_pcm_s": 3.2, "relay_first_audio_ms": 592, "spoken_s": 3.96, "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Yarg and Gevrek are cheeses from **Cornwall**.", "expert_answer": "Yarg and Gevrek are cheeses from **Cornwall**.", "expert_latency_s": 4.2, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 1684}
{"id": "q0374", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 4.74, "n_chunks": 5, "scores": [0.9719, 0.742, 0.8048, 0.7063, 0.7999], "eot_score": 0.7029, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "GREAT DANE", "query": "What breed of dog is Marmaduke in the newspaper cartoon strip of that name?", "transcript": "What breed of dog is Marmaduke in the newspaper cartoon strip of that name?", "first_audio_ms": 21, "stall_pcm_s": 3.2, "relay_first_audio_ms": 583, "spoken_s": 3.16, "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Oh, I see. Marmaduke is a Great Dane.", "expert_answer": "Marmaduke is a **Great Dane**.", "expert_latency_s": 1.24, "stall_ms": 21, "relay_ms": 1331}
{"id": "q0385", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 1.45, "n_chunks": 2, "scores": [0.9981, 0.6328], "eot_score": 0.3304, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Toy", "query": "What is a Jacob's Ladder?", "transcript": "What is a Jacob's Ladder?", "first_audio_ms": 551, "spoken_s": 43.36, "mode": "local", "answer": "A **Jacob's Ladder** can refer to different things depending on the context. Here are the most common meanings across various fields and traditions, particularly in religion, literature, folklore, and sometimes technology or design. The name often evokes imagery of ascent, spiritual journey, or transformation due to its symbolic associations and visual form—like a ladder reaching toward the sky with steps ascending higher than those below, reminiscent of light or energy radiating upward, as described in some interpretations from the Bible or poetry by William Blake, who famously wrote about it symbolizing divine inspiration and transcendence through \"the flight of thought\" or imagination rising step by step into realms beyond human perception.", "answer_ms": 18078}
{"id": "q0391", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.15, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.667, 0.6836, 0.696, 0.5351], "eot_score": 0.4132, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Percy LeBaron Spencer", "query": "Who invented the microwave oven in 1945?", "transcript": "Who invented the microwave oven in nineteen forty five?", "first_audio_ms": 549, "spoken_s": 17.88, "mode": "local", "answer": "The microwave oven was invented by Percy Spencer in 1945. While working at Raytheon, he discovered that microwaves could heat food when a radar magnetron accidentally melted a candy bar near him. This led to the development of the first microwave oven for cooking and heating food.", "answer_ms": 7435}
{"id": "q0405", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.04, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.9995, 0.1889, 0.4596], "eot_score": 0.1086, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": null, "query": "How many months have 28 days?", "transcript": "How many months have twenty eight days?", "first_audio_ms": 545, "spoken_s": 25.92, "mode": "local", "answer": "All 12 months have **at least 28 days**. However, if the question is asking how many months have **exactly 28 days**, then only **February** has exactly 28 days in common years and 29 in leap years. So strictly speaking, **only 1 month**—February—has exactly 28 days most of the time. But all months have **at least** 28 days.", "answer_ms": 10881}
{"id": "q0414", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 5.67, "n_chunks": 6, "scores": [0.974, 0.978, 0.6107, 0.5452, 0.4946, 0.425], "eot_score": 0.3586, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Imagine you are the last person on Earth. Write a diary entry describing your thoughts and feelings.", "transcript": "Imagine you are the last person on Earth. Write a diary entry describing your thoughts and feelings.", "first_audio_ms": 553, "spoken_s": 4.04, "mode": "local", "answer": "**Diary Entry – Day 4,217**", "answer_ms": 1578}
{"id": "q0424", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.42, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.9998, 0.6146, 0.4168], "eot_score": 0.0711, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Give me some examples of metamorphic rocks.", "transcript": "Give me some examples of metamorphic rocks.", "first_audio_ms": 558, "spoken_s": 36.72, "mode": "local", "answer": "Sure! Here are some common examples of metamorphic rocks, along with a brief description of how they form or their key characteristics. These rocks form from the transformation of existing rocks—igneous, sedimentary, or even other metamorphic rocks—due to heat, pressure, or chemically active fluids deep within the Earth's crust over long periods of time, without melting completely into magma. This process is called metamorphism, and it can cause changes in mineral composition, texture, and structure but not always preserve the original rock type entirely.", "answer_ms": 15068}
{"id": "q0435", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 1.98, "n_chunks": 2, "scores": [0.7415, 0.882], "eot_score": 0.8804, "eot_read_ms": 23, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Who are the top NFL Quarterbacks?", "transcript": "Who are the top NFL quarterbacks?", "first_audio_ms": 28, "stall_pcm_s": 3.2, "relay_first_audio_ms": 648, "spoken_s": 33.6, "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Based on recent seasons, the top NFL quarterbacks include Patrick Mahomes of the Chiefs, Josh Allen with the Bills, and Lamar Jackson from the Ravens. Joe Burrow in Cincinnati, Jalen Hurts for the Eagles, and Justin Herbert with the Chargers are also among the elite. C.J. Stroud has made an impact early in his career with the Texans, while Dak Prescott and Matthew Stafford have remained consistent leaders at their respective teams. Aaron Rodgers is still highly regarded despite changing teams. These rankings can shift based on performance each year, but these names consistently come up as top-tier QBs.", "expert_answer": "As of recent NFL seasons, the top quarterbacks are generally considered to include:\n\n1. **Patrick Mahomes — Kansas City Chiefs**\n2. **Josh Allen — Buffalo Bills**\n3. **Lamar Jackson — Baltimore Ravens**\n4. **Joe Burrow — Cincinnati Bengals**\n5. **Jalen Hurts — Philadelphia Eagles**\n6. **Justin Herbert — Los Angeles Chargers**\n7. **C.J. Stroud — Houston Texans**\n8. **Dak Prescott — Dallas Cowboys**\n9. **Matthew Stafford — Los Angeles Rams**\n10. **Aaron Rodgers — New York Jets**\n\nIf ranking by career legacy, **Mahomes, Rodgers, Stafford, and Russell Wilson** would be higher. If ranking by current form and upside, **Mahomes, Allen, Jackson, Burrow, Stroud, and Herbert** are usually near the top.", "expert_latency_s": 5.96, "stall_ms": 28, "relay_ms": 14999}
{"id": "q0447", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 1.94, "n_chunks": 2, "scores": [0.7307, 0.5135], "eot_score": 0.3541, "eot_read_ms": 22, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Can I run MacOS on a Windows PC?", "transcript": "Can I run Mac OS on a Windows PC?", "first_audio_ms": 592, "spoken_s": 31.84, "mode": "local", "answer": "You cannot natively run macOS on a Windows PC, as macOS is designed exclusively for Apple hardware and requires specific security and hardware features that are not present in standard Windows PCs. However, there are some workarounds depending on your needs and technical skills. Here are a few options you might consider, with important caveats and warnings about risks like malware or system instability. Always use caution when modifying operating systems or running unofficial tools like virtualization software on untrusted sources.", "answer_ms": 13264}
{"id": "q0459", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.27, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [1.0, 0.7115, 0.6782, 0.6254], "eot_score": 0.235, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What are some basic spirits you should have at your bar", "transcript": "What are some basic spirits you should have at your bar?", "first_audio_ms": 553, "spoken_s": 68.88, "mode": "local", "answer": "Having a solid foundation of basic spirits is essential for any home bar or mixology setup. Here are some key spirits you should consider having on hand to create a wide variety of cocktails and drinks, regardless of the occasion or style of serving. These can be stored in a well-ventilated area like a pantry or under-counter storage since they’re not typically refrigerated unless aged or served chilled regularly in certain cases like whiskey or vodka with ice cream applications—though most standard spirits don’t need cold storage until ready to use or serve chilled drinks specifically made from them such as martinis or old fashioneds where temperature matters more than ambient storage conditions due to their nature being distilled rather than fermented which makes proper aging less critical compared to wine or beer storage needs but still important for maintaining quality over time especially when opening frequently used bottles regularly so keeping them organized and easily accessible is key too alongside basic spirits here’s what you might want next to round out your bar setup properly ensuring versatility across different drink styles without overcomplicating things at first stage while building up gradually based on personal taste preferences over time.", "answer_ms": 29390}
{"id": "q0463", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.49, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.7047, 0.6711, 0.6281], "eot_score": 0.4876, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Does Las Vegas have a professional hockey team?", "transcript": "Does Las Vegas have a professional hockey team?", "first_audio_ms": 552, "spoken_s": 23.56, "mode": "local", "answer": "Yes, Las Vegas has a professional hockey team! The **Las Vegas Golden Knights** are an NHL team based in the city. They were founded in 2017 as an expansion team and became the 31st franchise in the National Hockey League. The Golden Knights play their home games at T-Mobile Arena in Downtown Las Vegas and have quickly become one of the league's most popular and successful teams, especially known for their passionate fan base and exciting style of play.", "answer_ms": 10200}
{"id": "q0471", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.49, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.9965, 0.7382, 0.5458, 0.5522], "eot_score": 0.3898, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Write a brief summary of Nezami Ganjavi's Layli and Majnun.", "transcript": "Nizami Ganjavi's Layli and Majnun.", "first_audio_ms": 553, "spoken_s": 46.28, "mode": "local", "answer": "*Nazami Ganjavi's \"Layli and Majnun\"* is a celebrated Persian poetic drama that tells the tragic love story of Layli, a beautiful woman from a noble family, and Majnun, a passionate poet deeply in love with her. Despite their intense emotional connection, societal norms prevent them from being together. The narrative blends lyrical poetry with dramatic elements, exploring themes of forbidden love, longing, separation, and spiritual devotion. Set in an idealized past, the work reflects both the beauty and pain of romantic love, showcasing Nizami’s mastery of verse and storytelling in classical Persian literature.", "answer_ms": 19692}
{"id": "q0484", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.77, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.562, 0.6821, 0.6401], "eot_score": 0.2939, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": null, "query": "电动汽车是智能交通的未来。", "transcript": "电动汽车是智能交通的未来。", "first_audio_ms": 556, "spoken_s": 38.12, "mode": "local", "answer": "电动汽车是智能交通的重要组成部分，但它们本身并不是智能交通的全部。智能交通系统依赖于先进的通信技术、数据分析、自动驾驶和基础设施优化，而电动汽车因其零排放、高能效和可与智能系统集成的特点，为实现更高效、安全和可持续的城市交通提供了重要支持。因此，电动汽车是推动智能交通发展的重要力量，但未来智能交通的实现还需要政策、技术、能源和城市规划等多方面的协同推进。", "answer_ms": 15511}
{"id": "q0490", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 1.8, "n_chunks": 2, "scores": [1.0, 0.6521], "eot_score": 0.6126, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": null, "query": "制定可追溯性计划。", "transcript": "制定可追溯性计划。", "first_audio_ms": 581, "spoken_s": 21.44, "mode": "local", "answer": "制定可追溯性计划是确保产品从原材料采购到最终交付给消费者整个过程中信息透明、责任明确的关键步骤。以下是一个系统化的可追溯性计划制定框架，适用于制造业、食品加工、医药等行业。可根据具体行业和企业需求进行调整和细化。", "answer_ms": 8714}
{"id": "q0495", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.96, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [1.0, 0.7566, 0.7597, 0.4621], "eot_score": 0.3748, "eot_read_ms": 22, "reference_answer": null, "query": "创建一个程序将动物分类到不同的组中。", "transcript": "创建一个程序将动物分类到不同的组中。", "first_audio_ms": 596, "spoken_s": 32.96, "mode": "local", "answer": "当然！下面是一个简单的 Python 代码示例，用于将动物分类到不同的组中，例如哺乳动物、鸟类、爬行动物、两栖动物和鱼类。我们可以使用一个字典来存储动物及其所属类别，然后编写函数来展示分类结果或根据输入进行分类判断。这个程序可以扩展为更复杂的系统，比如基于特征的自动分类，但这里我们先从基础的分类开始实现一个简单的交互式分类器和展示功能。", "answer_ms": 14198}
{"id": "q0506", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.33, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.9999, 0.5105, 0.5059], "eot_score": 0.067, "eot_read_ms": 23, "reference_answer": null, "query": "为什么自我关怀很重要？", "transcript": "为什么自我关怀很重要？", "first_audio_ms": 577, "spoken_s": 97.12, "mode": "local", "answer": "自我关怀非常重要，因为它有助于我们建立更健康、更积极的心理状态和生活方式。以下是几个关键原因，说明为什么自我关怀如此重要：1. 提升心理健康：自我关怀包括接纳自己的情绪、善待自己，而不是苛责或压抑。这有助于减少焦虑、抑郁和压力，增强心理韧性。2. 提高情绪调节能力：当我们学会对自己温柔以待，更容易识别和处理负面情绪，而不是逃避或压抑它们。3. 促进身心健康：关心自己的身体需求——如充足睡眠、均衡饮食、适度运动——有助于预防疾病，提升整体健康水平。4. 提升自尊与自信：持续的自我关怀能帮助我们建立更积极的自我形象，减少自我批评，从而增强自信心和内在价值感。5. 更好地应对挑战：当我们在困难面前对自己温柔，更容易坚持下去，保持动力，而不是轻易放弃。6. 为他人关怀打下基础：只有当我们先照顾好自己，才能更有能力去关心和帮助他人。就像“杯子满水”的比喻：你得先给自己倒水，才能给别人。总之，自我关怀不是自私，而是一种必要的自我照顾，是实现幸福、平衡和成长的重要基石。", "answer_ms": 40272}
